%region LongTablePageParts
% 🧩 longtable stores its head as a box and copies that same box onto every
% page, so a hierarchy chip inside the stored head can never advance from :1 to
% :2. Store a title-only chrome row in \LT@head to reserve the exact repeated
% head height, then overlay the numbered cap live whenever longtable inserts that
% box. The page-part counter advances once per physical table page while the
% register key remains unsuffixed.
