% ?? Generic multi-page table + avatar band row, for report appendices (e.g. a
% project catalogue) that need more columns or rows than the register/
% reference/glossary long tables above hardcode. Mirrors their structure ?
% \semio@table@long@render underneath ? but takes the colspec and header row
% as plain arguments instead of a fixed three-column shape.
\ExplSyntaxOn

% ?? The colspec and header are built here, inside the package, from plain
% arguments ? never from hand-written strings containing `\semio@...` names.
% Those names are only valid where `@` is catcode-11 (package files); a
% report's own content file (\input after \begin{document}) does not have
% that, so building them in the caller's source would silently break.
% Keeping composition inside the package is the fix, not a `\makeatletter`
% workaround at every call site.
%
% ?? The finished head is copied into a plain (non-expl3) macro and that bare
% macro *name* ? not its pre-expanded value ? is what reaches
% \semio@table@long@render, exactly like \SemioTableRegister passes
% \semio@register@table@header. longtable re-invokes the head macro itself on
% every page break; if a body row uses \multicolumn (as band rows do),
% pre-flattening the head's tokens into the argument list (via \exp_args:NV
% or similar) desyncs longtable's column bookkeeping and throws a "Misplaced
% \omit" the next time the header repeats. A colspec has no such issue since
% array fully expands it while parsing the preamble either way.
\tl_new:N \l_semio_table_long_colspec_tl
